  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "Evidence: Only one experiment (config_009) is complete, yielding 42.1% accuracy with multimodal singleprofile (scgpt + resnet50, weighted fusion). This is a single data point, so uncertainty is high about which design dimensions matter most. Question: config_019 is a minimal, controlled extension of config_009—identical encoders (scgpt, resnet50) and fusion (weighted)—but switches from singleprofile to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation. This isolates the effect of multi-profile aggregation, which is a core design choice in cellular profiling and likely a major source of signal. Why this is the best next step: (1) It directly exploits the one data point we have by testing the most impactful architectural change while holding all else constant, giving a clean read on whether multiprofile helps. (2) If accuracy improves substantially, the remaining 7 experiments can exploit multiprofile with better encoders/aggregation; if it does not, we pivot to modality or encoder choices. (3) Cost: multiprofile with avgpool adds moderate overhead over singleprofile (no transformer), so expected training cost is roughly 1.4–1.7 GPU hours—only ~30-50% more than config_009's 1.08 h—keeping total spend low while resolving a key uncertainty early in the budget."
}

